member.summary:
Fluent factory for rule condition expressions. Maps Firestore's vocabulary to C#:
// resource.data.ownerId == request.auth.uid Expr.Resource("data","ownerId").Eq(Expr.Auth("uid"))
// resource.data.public == true || resource.data.ownerId == request.auth.uid Expr.Any( Expr.Resource("data","public").Eq(true), Expr.Resource("data","ownerId").Eq(Expr.Auth("uid")))

Fluent builder for a :

var rules = RulesetBuilder.Build(r =>
    r.Match("users/{userId}", u =>
    {
        u.Allow(RuleOperations.Read, Expr.Auth("uid").Eq(Expr.Param("userId")));
        u.Allow(RuleOperations.Write, Expr.Auth("uid").Eq(Expr.Param("userId")));
        u.Match("posts/{postId}", p =>
            p.Allow(RuleOperations.Read, Expr.Const(true)));
    }));
